"A Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász (https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.05339)\nciteturn4academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Title: A Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász\nAuthors: Alexander Clow, Penny Haxell, Bojan Mohar\nTitle: A Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász\nAuthors: Alexander Clow, Penny Haxell, Bojan Mohar\nDate: Thu May  8 15:28:47 2025\n\nIn 1975 Lov\\'{a}sz conjectured that every $r$-partite, $r$-uniform hypergraph contains $r-1$ vertices whose deletion reduces the matching number. If true, this statement would imply a well-known conjecture of Ryser from 1971, which states that every $r$-partite, $r$-uniform hypergraph has a vertex cover of size at most $r-1$ times its matching number. When $r=2$, Ryser's conjecture is simply K\\H{o}nig's theorem, and the conjecture of Lov\\'asz is an immediate corollary. Ryser's conjecture for $r=3$ was proven by Aharoni in 2001, and remains open for all $r\\geq 4$. Here we show that the conjecture of Lov\\'asz is false in the case $r=3$. Our counterexample is the line hypergraph of the Biggs-Smith graph, a highly symmetric cubic graph on 102 vertices.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász - researchr publication authors (https://researchr.org/publication/ClowHM26/authors)\nciteturn4search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # A Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász\n\nAlexander Clow, Penny Haxell, Bojan Mohar. A Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász.\n\n  * DOI\n\n# Statistics\n\n  * References: 0\n  * Cited by: 0\n  * Reviews: 0\n  * Bibliographies: 0\n\n# PDF\n\n  * [Upload PDF for personal use]\n\n\n# A Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász\n\nAlexander Clow, Penny Haxell, Bojan Mohar. A Counterexample to a Conjecture of Lovász. Combinatorica, 46(4):26, August 2026. [doi]\n\n  * Abstract\n  * Authors\n  * BibTeX\n  * References\n  * Bibliographies\n  * Reviews\n  *   * ## Authors\n\n### 